        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>How much is the Horizon 7.4 AT?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On 21 November 2026 Amazon showed it at $1,499.99, and Horizon's store listed $1,799 against a $2,399 regular price, with a one-day code taking it to $1,499. Horizon's prices change often, so compare both.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the difference between the Horizon 7.0 AT and 7.4 AT?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The 7.4 AT has a 22-inch-wide deck (the 7.0 is 20), a 350 lb capacity (325), a heart-rate chest strap, a Sprint 8 program, and five years on parts with two of labour (three and one). Speed and incline are the same. The 7.0 AT has Apple Watch, Galaxy Watch and GymKit support; the 7.4 does not.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does the Horizon 7.4 AT fold?</h3></summary>
